SUMMARY:Yin Yoga with Sound Bath - Cami
LOCATION:Paths to Restoration\, 107 Montrose Ave\, Lafayette
DESCRIPTION:Slow down\, settle into the moment\, and discover the power of 
 stillness.\nYin Yoga is a slow\, meditative practice that invites you to h
 old gentle poses for several minutes\, allowing you to gradually work into
  the body's deeper connective tissues. Rather than flowing from pose to po
 se\, you'll be encouraged to breathe\, observe\, and explore your own edge
  with patience and mindfulness.\nAs you remain in each posture\, you'll ha
 ve the opportunity to notice areas of tension\, practice staying present t
 hrough mild discomfort\, and cultivate greater flexibility\, self-awarenes
 s\, and inner calm. Throughout class\, your instructor will offer gentle g
 uidance to help quiet the mind and support your experience.\nThe practice 
 concludes with an immersive sound bath during Savasana\, the final resting
  pose. Crystal singing bowls\, Tibetan singing bowls\, gongs\, and other t
 herapeutic sound instruments create a rich landscape of resonant tones tha
 t encourage deep relaxation and a peaceful transition into rest.\nWhether 
 you're looking to improve mobility\, reduce stress\, or simply carve out t
 ime to reconnect with yourself\, this class offers a space to slow down\, 
 breathe deeply\, and leave feeling refreshed and restored.\nNo prior yoga 
 experience is necessary. All bodies and experience levels are welcome.\n\n
